  "facts": [
    "Opened January 15, 1963, the Alexander Hamilton Bridge instantly linked the Trans‑Manhattan Expressway in Washington Heights with the Cross Bronx Expressway, becoming a vital artery for I‑95 and US 1 traffic.",
    "Spanning 2,375 feet, the bridge’s 555‑foot steel arch provides 103 feet of vertical clearance, while its iconic spiraling ramps—nicknamed “The Corkscrew”—connect to the Major Deegan Expressway and Harlem River Drive.",
    "Renovated from 2009 to 2014, China Construction America finished the $407 million overhaul 35 days ahead of schedule and under budget, earning praise for keeping the bridge operational during the upgrade."
